Hand fixes to the GENERATED C sources, applied on top of the generators' output.
================================================================================

The committed generated sources carry fixes the generators cannot express (see
issues/closed/generated-sources-drift.issue):
  - built_in_functions.c: kernel_TYPEP resolves symbol type specifiers to
    classes; kernel_SET_SYMBOL_{PACKAGE,VALUE,FUNCTION,PLIST} call the C
    setters in their real (object, new-value) argument order; the
    kernel_structure_functions.h / bytecode.h / packages.h includes.
  - kernel_structure_functions.{c,h}: the hot-3 CONS representation of
    LEXICAL-VARIABLE (one allocation, car/cdr access) and the hot-2 _fast
    accessors.
  - structure_functions.c: the GC-rootset pinning of the structure classes in
    kernel_initialize_structure_functions.

`make regenerate` regenerates the pristine output and then applies this patch
(patch -p1 from the repository root), so regeneration is REPRODUCIBLE and a
generator-spec change shows up as a clean diff.  If the patch ever fails to
apply, the generators' output shifted: re-derive this file by committing the
intended final sources, running the bare generation, and capturing
`git diff -R` over the generated files (then restore).

Everything below this line is the unified diff (old = pristine generator
output, new = the fixed sources).
